# marker  load-use  redirects  case
1 0 0 setup
2 0 0 EX/MEM -> EX, rs1
3 0 0 EX/MEM -> EX, rs2
4 0 0 EX/MEM -> EX, rs3 (DOT4.S8 accumulator)
5 0 0 MEM/WB -> EX, rs1
6 0 0 MEM/WB -> EX, rs2
7 0 0 MEM/WB -> EX, rs3
8 0 0 register-file bypass, rs1/rs2 and rs3
9 0 0 EX/MEM wins over MEM/WB
10 1 0 load-use, rs1
11 1 0 load-use, rs2
12 1 0 load-use, rs3
13 1 0 load, then store of the loaded register
14 0 0 load to x0: no stall
15 0 0 rs3 only counts when read: addi into the loaded register
16 0 0 load, then a use two later: MEM/WB, no stall
17 0 0 branch not taken
18 0 1 branch taken: the two behind it are flushed
19 0 1 branch on forwarded operands
20 0 1 jal, and a use of its link register
21 0 1 jalr with a forwarded base
22 1 1 jalr with its base from a load
23 0 0 8 x DOT4.S8 into one accumulator: no stall
24 0 0 CLIP.S8 right after DOT4.S8
25 0 0 writes to x0 are not forwarded
26 0 0 multiply result forwarded
27 1 0 store data forwarded, then load and use
